# Regression fixture: an explicit `init` (body form) with a `Trait'owned`
# parameter that defaults to a call returning a bare trait type. Mirrors
# `@inject`'s own (docs/book.md §33)
# `'owned` transient-dependency case — `@inject`'s own desugar_inject.rs
# synthesizes exactly this shape (an init with an `'owned`-typed param), so
# a bug in emitting it blocks `@inject` even though the bug has nothing to
# do with dependency injection itself.
#
# Was two compounding transpiler bugs, both in `emit_init`'s "Body init"
# path (`src/transpiler/emit_struct.rs`) and `struct_init_defaults`
# (`src/transpiler/mod.rs`):
#   1. The init param's own type got boxed twice: `Greeter'owned greeter`
#      emitted as `Box<Box<dyn Greeter>>` instead of `Box<dyn Greeter>`
#      (`emit_type`'s `Type::Qualified(_, OwnerQual::Owned)` arm called
#      `emit_named_type` -- which already returns `Box<dyn Trait>` for a
#      trait name -- and then wrapped that again in `Box<...>`).
#   2. The default expression (`freshGreeter()`, returning bare `impl
#      Greeter` static dispatch, not `Box<dyn Greeter>`) was never wrapped
#      in `Box::new(...)` at the omitting call site, because
#      `struct_init_defaults` rendered each default with the qualifier-blind
#      `emit_expr` instead of the qualifier-aware `emit_let_value`.
#
# A third, previously-latent bug surfaced once the above two were fixed and
# this could compile far enough to hit codegen's derive logic: a bare or
# `'owned`-qualified trait field (`Box<dyn Trait>`) was never excluded from
# the struct's auto-derived `Clone`/`PartialEq`/`Debug` the way a `[Trait]`
# array field already was (`emit_struct.rs`'s `has_non_clone_field`/
# `has_non_debug_trait_array_field`) -- `dyn Greeter` implements none of
# those, so the struct failed to compile (E0277/E0369) even with a single,
# correctly-typed `Box<dyn Greeter>` field.

trait Greeter:
    req string greet()

struct EnglishGreeter as Greeter:
    req string greet(): "hello"

Greeter freshGreeter():
    EnglishGreeter()

struct Greeting:
    Greeter'owned greeter

    init(Greeter'owned greeter = freshGreeter()):
        self.greeter = greeter

    req string say():
        self.greeter.greet()

def main():
    let g = Greeting()
    print g.say()
